course: dictionary
lesson: 12749
title: Slang and casual words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Slang is casual, everyday talk that friends use. You will not find slang in a formal letter, but you will hear it in chats and stories. «Dude» is one of these words. Context helps you find its meaning.
explain: «Hey, dude, can you wait for me?» Here dude is a friendly way to talk to a friend. «Dude! I just scored a goal!» Here dude is a shout of excitement, so it is an interjection. «He is a cool dude» means a cool man or boy.
explain: Dude is most common in American and Canadian talk. In other places, people may use it less. If you are not sure what a slang word means, check the words around it and then look it up in a dictionary.
fact: Slang is informal, everyday language, not formal writing.
fact: «Dude» can mean a man or boy, or a friend you are talking to.
fact: «Dude!» can show surprise, excitement, or annoyance.
fact: «Dude ranch» means a holiday ranch for visitors from the city.
fact: Use slang with friends, but choose plain words in formal writing for school.
exercise: «Hey, dude, do you want to play?» What does dude mean here? | A type of food | A school bell | * A friend | A big, old house
exercise: «Dude! I just won the race!» What does dude show? | * Surprise and excitement | Tiredness | Confusion about the rules | Sadness
exercise: «The dude in the red cap waved at us.» What is the dude? | A cloud | A dog | * A man or boy | A bird
test: «Hey, dude, can I borrow your pencil?» What does dude mean here? | * A friend | A teacher | A sandwich | A bird
test: Why is «dude» called slang? | * It is informal, everyday talk | It is a number | It is the name of a country | It is a formal word used in official letters
exam: What is a «dude ranch»? | A school for horses | * A holiday ranch for visitors from the city | A race track | A shop that sells fancy clothes
